Read the last letter of the previous token and the first of the current
one. The 'a' response favors short fragments and is weaker if the next
letter is labial too. Other vowels give small, sometimes negative signals.
Accents and selected spelling counterparts share the same letter rules.
This approximates the dominant training pattern, not lexical exceptions.
