"""Approximate a demonstrative/clause-linking word detector.

'That' is strongest (especially capitalized); 'this', 'what', 'while',
and several translations have smaller responses. Lowercase 'that' is
attenuated after reporting/thinking words and in 'such that', but enhanced
after coordination or punctuation. Case and attached punctuation matter.
Only the current and preceding tokens in the same document are examined.
Unlisted words are zero: this leaves small, scattered responses unexplained.
"""
READS = ()
# Demonstratives, relative/interrogative words, and subordinators.
WORDS = {
    'this': 1.03, 'these': 0.94, 'those': 0.64, 'thats': 2.14,
    'what': 0.96, 'whatever': 1.10, 'which': 0.34,
    'whether': 0.83, 'while': 1.10, 'whilst': 1.06,
    'because': 0.67, 'although': 0.48, 'though': 0.46,
    'whereas': 0.40, 'where': -0.15, 'how': -0.10, 'who': -0.08,
    'que': 0.57, 'che': 0.67, 'dass': 1.40, 'daß': 1.30,
    'das': 0.48, 'dat': 1.65, 'что': 1.14, 'это': 0.51,
    'cette': 0.41, 'questo': 0.75, 'dieses': 0.76,
    'この': 0.69, 'その': 0.46, 'それ': 0.76, '该': 0.95,
}
